president biden is in belgium meeting  with our nato g7 and european union  allies they're looking for the best way  to help ukraine without escalating the  war one month into the conflict we're  seeing new signs that ukraine is holding  off russian advances into most of its  major cities and in some cases pushing  back russian troops from positions  they've held holly williams is inside  ukraine and ed o'keefe is with the  president in brussels let's begin with  you so what is the president doing this  morning  well vlad good to see you he's here at  nato headquarters meeting with the  leaders of the 29 other member nations  later he'll meet with leaders of the g7  and the european council all of this  designed to send a strong message of  defiance to russia's president vladimir  putin  we are united in condemning the  kremlin's unprovoked aggression  and in our support for ukraine's  sovereignty and territorial integrity  an extraordinary show of unity at nato  headquarters in belgium as the 30 member  states are here for their first  face-to-face talks about russian  aggression in ukraine this summit is set  to feature an address by ukrainian  president vladimir zielinski a major  test for the alliance as it grapples  with how to appropriately respond to the  invasion of his country which isn't a  nato member  nato's chief announced wednesday the  alliance is doubling its troop  deployment along its eastern flank  sending four new battle groups to  bulgaria hungary romania and slovakia  and today members are expected to agree  on even more for ukraine including  increased cyber security support and  equipment to protect against chemical  biological radiological and nuclear  threats  a white house official tells cbs news  that president biden's package of 800  million dollars in military assistance  to ukraine including anti-aircraft and  anti-tank systems began arriving in the  country on wednesday  and this state department now formally  believes russian forces 